---
// design/08_INVEST.md, ui_ux/08_INVEST_UI.md.
// No TAM figure, no projection sparklines, no simulated raise indicators — all explicitly
// forbidden by ui_ux/08. "What is open" (§4) must outweigh the metric bento visually; it is
// rendered larger and after the ladder, not squeezed beside the metrics.
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import DisclosurePanel from '../components/DisclosurePanel.astro';
import LadderSchematic from '../components/LadderSchematic.astro';
import FormField from '../components/FormField.astro';
import { solutions } from '../data/solutions';

const metrics = [
	{ figure: '+70.3 pp', label: 'Recovery advantage over standard networks' },
	{ figure: '383', label: 'Controlled experiments' },
	{ figure: '16,316', label: 'Lines of code' },
	{ figure: '7 / 1', label: 'Solutions specified / available now' },
];

const ladderRows = solutions.map((s) => ({
	name: s.name,
	price: s.pricing.map((p) => `${p.label}: ${p.amount}`).join(' · '),
	gate: s.gate ? s.gate.name : 'Available now',
}));

const raiseUses = [
	{
		title: 'The two validation studies',
		body: 'The monitoring lead-time measurement (~8 GPU-hours): does the health signal lead the global loss curve? The separation study (~20 GPU-hours): does inter-node disagreement separate mislabelled data from hard data? Both run on existing hardware. Capital accelerates the timeline.',
	},
	{
		title: 'The first three engagements',
		body: 'Turning "bookable" into "booked." Taking the first design partners through a full diagnostic, generating the first real non-CIFAR result, and publishing it with the partner.',
	},
	{
		title: 'The legal and regulatory consultations',
		body: 'Two consultations with months of lead time, both urgently needed: a regulatory consultant who has filed a change-control plan, and a data-protection lawyer who works in AI. Neither has been engaged.',
	},
	{
		title: 'The technical co-founder',
		body: 'One person is building this. Capital allows that person to be found rather than competed for later. The architecture is done; the company-building is not.',
	},
];
---

<Page title="THE INVESTMENT CASE">
	<section class="section container">
		<Eyebrow>THE INVESTMENT CASE</Eyebrow>
		<h1>
			ORMAS is a commercial primitive in a market that does not yet have one. The primitive
			works. The solutions are specified. The evidence is documented.
		</h1>
		<p class="invest-subhead">
			We are not asking anyone to believe the category exists. We are asking whether the
			evidence justifies a conversation.
		</p>
		<Button variant="primary" href="/contact">Request the full brief</Button>
	</section>

	<section class="section container">
		<div class="metric-bento">
			{
				metrics.map((m) => (
					<div class="metric-bento-cell">
						<p class="metric-bento-figure tabular">{m.figure}</p>
						<p class="metric-bento-label">{m.label}</p>
					</div>
				))
			}
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section container">
		<p class="invest-case">
			ORMAS is an architectural primitive — a constraint on how neural networks train — that
			gives every node of the network an independently addressable identity. That property
			does not exist in standard architectures. It cannot be approximated by post-hoc tools.
			It can only be built in, and it has been.
		</p>
		<p class="invest-case">
			The commercial consequence: a network with addressable nodes can protect regions,
			repair them, account for their activity, separate them by data source, and delete
			specific data contributions on request. Those five operations map directly onto five
			markets with clearly named buyers, documented pain, and published alternatives that are
			either absent or orders of magnitude more expensive than what this architecture makes
			possible.
		</p>
		<p class="invest-case">
			The evidence base for the primitive is 383 controlled experiments across four
			architecture families, adversarially tested by its own author's kill suite, with a
			preprint under review. That is an unusual artifact for an unfunded company. The
			question the raise answers is: what does this look like at scale?
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section container">
		<Eyebrow>THE SOLUTION LADDER</Eyebrow>
		<h2>Seven solutions. One available now, two open for pre-booking. One gate separates the tiers.</h2>
		<LadderSchematic />
		<div class="invest-ladder-detail">
			{
				ladderRows.map((row) => (
					<div class="invest-ladder-row">
						<p class="invest-ladder-name">{row.name}</p>
						<p class="invest-ladder-price tabular">{row.price}</p>
						<p class="invest-ladder-gate">{row.gate}</p>
					</div>
				))
			}
		</div>
		<p class="invest-ladder-note">All prices: designed, not yet tested against real customers.</p>
		<p class="invest-gate-summary">
			Four of the seven solutions depend on one validation study: a 20 GPU-hour run that
			tests whether the architecture's per-node readouts can separate mislabelled data from
			hard-but-correctly-labelled data. Pass: all seven solutions are reachable. Fail: four
			solutions close. The first three remain. The downside case is a working company, not
			zero.
		</p>
		<Button variant="tertiary" href="/solutions">See the full solution detail</Button>
	</section>

	<section class="section container">
		<Eyebrow>THE FIVE MARKETS</Eyebrow>
		<h2>Five markets. All reading the same record differently.</h2>
		<Button variant="tertiary" href="/sectors">Full market analysis</Button>
	</section>

	<section class="section container">
		<Eyebrow>THE LICENSING MOAT</Eyebrow>
		<h2>The engine is MIT. The moat is the record.</h2>
		<p class="invest-case">
			What compounds is not the code. The customer's accumulated record. Their calibrated
			bound. The fact that somebody signed it.
		</p>
		<Button variant="tertiary" href="/licensing">Full licensing detail</Button>
	</section>

	<section class="section container">
		<Eyebrow>WHAT THE RAISE IS FOR</Eyebrow>
		<h2>What this becomes with capital.</h2>
		<ol class="invest-raise-uses">
			{
				raiseUses.map((use, i) => (
					<li class="invest-raise-use">
						<span class="invest-raise-use-index">{i + 1}</span>
						<div>
							<p class="invest-raise-use-title">{use.title}</p>
							<p class="invest-raise-use-body">{use.body}</p>
						</div>
					</li>
				))
			}
		</ol>
	</section>

	<section class="section container invest-open">
		<Eyebrow>WHAT IS OPEN</Eyebrow>
		<h2>What is not known yet.</h2>
		<DisclosurePanel label="The honest section">
			<p>Zero customer conversations have happened.</p>
			<p>
				Every buyer title, price, and cycle length in the commercial plan is reasoned
				bottom-up from established spend on alternatives. None of it is tested against a
				real customer.
			</p>
			<p>The separation study has not been run.</p>
			<p>The monitoring lead time has not been measured.</p>
			<p>No regulatory consultant has read the specification.</p>
			<p>No data-protection lawyer has told us what may be certified.</p>
			<p>
				These are the four things the raise is for. If any of them produces a negative
				result, the plan is updated accordingly.
			</p>
			<p class="invest-open-closer">
				The research has been adversarially validated. The commercial thesis has not been
				tested at all.
			</p>
		</DisclosurePanel>
	</section>

	<section class="section container">
		<Eyebrow>IF THIS IS THE KIND OF THING YOU INVEST IN</Eyebrow>
		<p class="invest-case">
			We are open to conversations with investors who understand deep-tech primitives,
			long-cycle B2B markets, and the specific risk profile of a pre-revenue company with a
			validated research result but no customer conversations yet.
		</p>
		<p class="invest-case">
			We are not doing a general raise. If you want to see the full brief — the evidence, the
			model, the solution ladder, the financial assumptions, and the open questions — request
			it below. We will respond within a few days.
		</p>

		<form class="invest-form">
			<FormField id="invest-name" label="Name" />
			<FormField id="invest-email" label="Email" type="email" />
			<FormField id="invest-org" label="Fund / Organisation" />
			<FormField id="invest-thesis" label="What you invest in" />
			<Button variant="primary" type="submit">Request the brief</Button>
		</form>

		<p class="invest-form-note">
			We are not looking for a fast close. We are looking for the right partner. If that is
			you, we will spend the time to make it clear.
		</p>
	</section>
</Page>
